    "priority_and_provenance.md": "--- R1/priority_and_provenance.md\n+++ final/priority_and_provenance.md\n@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@\n \n ## Target\n \n-Invariant k405 in Reznik\u2013Garcia\u2013Koiller, *Fifty New Invariants of N-Periodics in the Elliptic Billiard*, Arnold Mathematical Journal 7 (2021), 341\u2013355, Table 5, p.348, DOI https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-021-00174-y. The arXiv companion is *Eighty New Invariants of N-Periodics in the Elliptic Billiard*, https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.12497v11, Table 5, printed p.7. The source asks for the constant antipedal vertex centroid at even N for the center and foci. Its initial setting is a pair of confocal ellipses. Its Section 3.7 uses central inversion of opposite vertices, supporting the explicit least-period parity convention here; the table itself does not formally define least period.\n+Invariant k405 in Reznik\u2013Garcia\u2013Koiller, *Fifty New Invariants of N-Periodics in the Elliptic Billiard*, Arnold Mathematical Journal 7 (2021), 341\u2013355, Table 5, p.348, DOI https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-021-00174-y. The arXiv companion's printed title is *Eighty New Invariants in the Elliptic Billiard*, https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.12497v11, Table 5, printed p.7 (the arXiv metadata uses the longer title *Eighty New Invariants of N-Periodics in the Elliptic Billiard*). The source asks for the constant antipedal vertex centroid at even N for the center and foci. Its initial setting is a pair of confocal ellipses. Its Section 3.7 uses central inversion of opposite vertices, supporting the explicit least-period parity convention here; the table itself does not formally define least period.\n \n ## Documented project record and exact later overlap\n \n"
